Good Morning,

 

Another spring-like day in South Carolina as we send our Thursday greetings.
Short photo flight at 10:00!

 

SPOTLITE:  Our Fun Stuff Joke ListT spotlite shines brightly today on Matt
Rassette, from Midland Michigan.  Matt celebrated his birthday yesterday,
and is in England this week on assignment with the Dow Chemical Company.
Due to the time difference between here and England, we decided to wait to
make sure all of the police reports were in and to confirm that Matt had
indeed survived his birthday yesterday in Jolly old England.    

 

We will not tell you how old Matt is, as your editor learned long ago not to
get on the wrong side of an International Man of Intrigue, who has business
connections all over the world.  Happy Birthday, Matt!

 

In other important news, your editor and two pilot neighbors visited the
indoor range yesterday.  My target:

 

cid:Image_00_DSC06553.jpg

 

9mm, 17 round magazine.  Holes in rings 6 & 7 were due to bad bullets.  J

 

Our joke today comes from our friends at Clean Laughs.

 

Keep smiling...........ss

 

****************************************************************************
**************************

 

                                                SIGHTSEEING AT ALCATRAZ 

A couple with three children waited in line at San Francisco's Pier 41 to
purchase tickets for a sightseeing boat to Alcatraz Prison. The children
weren't good at waiting: they fidgeted, whined, and punched one another. The
frazzled parents reprimanded them to no avail.

Finally they reached the ticket window.

"Five tickets, please," the father said. "Two round trip, three one way."

 

Steve Sanderson

Gilbert, South Carolina 29054

